From 3a00450fe101b254c9946859baa9b979e26f0b19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:47:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(journal): open a ready New Entry form on landing,
 auto-default single bank/cash account, paginate the list
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three related UX changes to Journal Entries, all confirmed against a
Before/After mockup shown to the user first:

- Landing on the page (nothing selected yet) now shows a blank New Entry
  form instead of an empty "select an entry" placeholder — the same form
  "+ New" already opened, just shown by default. renderEmpty() is removed
  as dead code now that nothing renders it.
- When there's exactly one bank account (or one cash account) configured,
  it's auto-selected for a Bank/Cash voucher instead of asking the user to
  pick from a single-option dropdown. Applies when opening a new entry and
  when switching voucher class.
- The entries list was silently capped at the backend's default page size
  (50) with no way to see older entries. Added cursor-based pagination
  ("← Newer" / "Older →"), matching the existing convention in
  AuditLogPage.tsx. Any filter, search, or type change resets back to the
  first page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TzRYcGBjDHGFFNgpNih7vR
---
 .../pages/accounting/JournalEntriesPage.tsx   | 108 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 94 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

